          %title Toposes are extensive
          %h1#toposes_are_extensive Toposes are extensive
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#statement"} Statement
              %li
                %a{:href => "#proofs"} Proofs
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#from_finitary_to_infinitary"} From finitary to infinitary
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#via_pushouts_of_monos"} Via pushouts of monos
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#via_quasidisjointness"} Via quasi-disjointness
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#via_logical_functors"} Via logical functors
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#statement Statement
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+topos"} elementary topos
            is a finitary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+category"} extensive category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
            indexed by any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arity+class"} arity class
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "-extensive." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
          %h2#proofs Proofs
          %p
            There are several possible proofs. In all cases, stability of coproducts under pullback is automatic since a topos is locally cartesian closed, so it suffices to consider
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+coproduct"} disjointness
          %h3#from_finitary_to_infinitary From finitary to infinitary
          %p
            As shown at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+category"} extensive category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+logic"} classical logic
            then
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi j
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊔
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⊔
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo ≠
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_{j\in J} A_j \cong A_1 \sqcup A_2 \sqcup \coprod_{j\neq 1,2} A_j
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+logic"} constructive logic
            and so this argument does not apply.
          %p Nevertheless, we mention a couple of proofs that apparently apply only to the finitary case in addition to the fully general version.
          %h3#via_pushouts_of_monos Via pushouts of monos
          %p
            A proof applying to finite coproducts is given in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone"} Johnstone, A2.4.4
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\to X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\to Y
            are monic, it suffices to show that the pushout of a mono is a mono and also a pullback.
          %p
            To see this, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↣
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\rightarrowtail B
            be monic and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:A\to C
            any morphism, and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:B\to P C
            be the name of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo ×
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,g):A\to B\times C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,g)
            is the pullback
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %mo ↣
                  %mi P
                  %mi C
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \in_C \rightarrowtail P C \times C
            along
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (h,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mi l
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k,l):X\to B\times C
            factors through
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,g)
            iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi h
                  %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mi l
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (h k,l)
            factors through
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \in_C
            (i.e.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi l
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi h
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l(x) \in h k(x)
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:X
            in the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi l
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h k = \{\} \circ l
            (i.e.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi l
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h k(x) = \{l(x)\}
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:X
            in the internal logic), which implies that the square
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi h
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                          %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \array{A &amp; \xrightarrow{g} &amp; C \\ ^f\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\{\}} \\ B &amp; \xrightarrow{h} &amp; P C }
          %p is a pullback.
          %p Now given a pushout
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi d
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi c
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \array{A &amp; \xrightarrow{g} &amp; C \\ ^f\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{d} \\ B &amp; \xrightarrow{c} &amp; D }
          %p
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            monic, with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            as above we have an induced
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m:D \to P C
            by the universal property of the pushout, with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m d = \{\}
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mi c
                    %mo =
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m c = h
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\}
            is monic,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            must also be monic, and since the previous square is a pullback, so must this one be.
          %h3#via_quasidisjointness Via quasi-disjointness
          %p
            A different proof applying to finite coproducts can be obtained by combining A1.5.14 and A1.6.2 of
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone"} Johnstone
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            to make the following squares pullbacks:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi R
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi r
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ←
                            %mi s
                        %mtd
                          %mi S
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mrow
                              %mi r
                              %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi i
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi i
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                          %mo +
                          %mi B
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ←
                            %mi j
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{ R &amp; \xrightarrow{r} &amp; A &amp; \xleftarrow{s} &amp; S\\
                  ^{r'}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^i &amp;&amp; \downarrow\\
                  A &amp; \xrightarrow{i} &amp; A+B &amp; \xleftarrow{j} &amp; B}
          %p
            Specifically,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi r
                  %mo ,
                  %mi r
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (r,r')
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pair"} kernel pair
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ▵
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \triangle : A \to R
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ▵
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \triangle = 1_A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi r
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (r,s)
            is a coproduct diagram. Thus, the pair of morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_R:R\to R
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ▵
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi s
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \triangle \circ s : S\to R
            factor (uniquely) through some
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:A\to R
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mi r
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h r = 1_R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo :
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r:R\to A
            has both a left and a right inverse, so it is an isomorphism, and hence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            is monic. Dually,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            is monic.
          %p
            Now we claim that any two morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g:S\to X
            with domain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            are equal. For the pair of morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi r
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \xrightarrow{r} A \to A+X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \xrightarrow{f} X \to A+X
            factor uniquely through
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            (which, recall, is the coproduct
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo +
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R+S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            is an isomorphism, this factorization must be the left coprojection
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo +
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to A+X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \xrightarrow{f} X \to A+X
            is equal to the composite
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi s
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo +
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \xrightarrow{s} A \to A+X
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi g
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo +
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \xrightarrow{g} X \to A+X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to A+X
            is monic by the previous paragraph,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f= g
          %p
            Finally, since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            is a strict initial object,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\to S
            is monic. And of course
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi S
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_S : S\to S
            is also monic, and these two monomorphisms are classified by two maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g:S\to \Omega
            into the subobject classifier. By the previous paragraph,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f= g
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ≅
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\cong 0
            and is initial.
          %h3#via_logical_functors Via logical functors
          %p
            Finally, we give a proof that applies constructively to arbitrary coproducts. This proof is due to Jibladze and can be found (in fibered-topos language) in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Streicher"} Streicher, Appendix A
          %p
            Suppose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            a topos with
            = succeed "-indexed" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            belonging to some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arity+class"} arity class
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta : \mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{E}^J
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logical+functor"} logical functor
            with a left adjoint
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_J
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone"} Johnstone
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logical+functor"} logical functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_J
            induces equivalences
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi j
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}^J/\{A_j\} \to \mathcal{E}/\coprod_j A_j
            (which is one characterization of
            = succeed "-extensivity)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_J
            to be faithful. As with any adjunction, to show the left adjoint to be faithful it suffices to show that the unit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                  %mo :
                  %mi Id
                  %mo →
                  %mi Δ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta : Id \to \Delta \coprod_J
            is monic, which means in this case that the injections
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi j
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi j
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_j \to \coprod_j A_j
            are all monic.
          %p
            Now since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi κ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            is an arity class,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo ×
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J\times J
            also belongs to it, and hence so do the fibers of the diagonal
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi J
                    %mo ×
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J\to J\times J
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            has coproducts indexed by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsingletons"} subsingletons
            determined by the equalities
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo =
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (j=k)
            for any
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j,k\in J
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            we can write
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_j = \coprod_{k\in J} \coprod_{(j=k)} A_{k}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi j
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi J
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_j \to \coprod_{k\in J} A_{k}
            is obtained by applying the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_J
            to the evident family of maps
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_{(j=k)} A_{k}\to A_k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_J
            is the left adjoint of a logical functor, it preserves monomorphisms (see A2.4.8 of
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone"} Johnstone
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logical+functor"} logical functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_{(j=k)} A_{k}\to A_k
            is monic.
          %p
            Now, the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_{(j=k)} : \mathcal{E}^{(j=k)} \to \mathcal{E}
            has a logical right adjoint sending
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\in\mathcal{E}
            to the subsingleton-indexed family
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{B\}_{(j=k)}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{A\}_{(j=k)} \to \{ \coprod_{(j=k)} A \}_{(j=k)}
            are isomorphisms (to define an inverse, it suffices to consider the object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_{(j=k)} A
            under the assumption
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j=k
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_{(j=k)}
            is fully faithful, and in particular faithful, and since its right adjoint is also logical, it induces an equivalence
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}^{(j=k)} \simeq \mathcal{E}/\coprod_{(j=k)} 1
          %p
            However, the unit of a pullback adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi I
                  %mo ⇄
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}/I \rightleftarrows \mathcal{E}
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to A\times I
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi I
                  %mo ×
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I\cong I\times I
            and thus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            is subterminal. Moreover, in this case the counits of the adjunction are the projections
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\times I \to A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I\to 1
            and therefore also monic. Finally, in our case where
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I = \coprod_{(j=k)} 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_k
            is precisely the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_{(j=k)} A_{k} \to A_k
            that we wanted to prove to be monic.
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Johnstone
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sketches+of+an+Elephant"} Sketches of an Elephant
            %li#Streicher
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Streicher"}> Thomas Streicher
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fibered categories a la Jean Benabou
                %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/citations;jsessionid=76DB3E2F57E81C74E05109B8F7E11E44?doi=10.1.1.678.919"} citeseer
